# TCP/IP Encapsulation and Network Communication Lab

## Overview

This lab demonstrates how data moves through the **TCP/IP model** using encapsulation and de-encapsulation.

The lab began by configuring two devices on the same IPv4 network and analyzing successful communication between them. Packet Tracer Simulation Mode was then used to examine how source and destination IP addresses, MAC addresses, and Protocol Data Units (PDUs) are used at different layers.

The destination IP address was later changed to place the destination on a different network. This demonstrated how a device uses its **subnet mask and routing information** to determine whether a destination is local or must be reached through a router.

