## Initial Network Configuration

The initial devices were configured with the following IPv4 addresses:

| Device | IP Address | Subnet Mask | Network |
|--------|------------|-------------|---------|
| PC1 | 192.168.1.10 | 255.255.255.0 | 192.168.1.0/24 |
| PC2 | 192.168.1.20 | 255.255.255.0 | 192.168.1.0/24 |

Both devices used a `/24` prefix.

A `/24` corresponds to the subnet mask:

`255.255.255.0`

This produced the network:

`192.168.1.0/24`

The usable host range is:

`192.168.1.1 - 192.168.1.254`

The broadcast address is:

`192.168.1.255`

---

## Same-Network Communication

PC1 was configured as:

`192.168.1.10/24`

PC2 was configured as:

`192.168.1.20/24`

Both addresses belong to:

`192.168.1.0/24`

Because both devices were members of the same network, they could communicate locally without requiring a router to forward traffic between networks.

The subnet mask allowed the devices to determine that the destination was part of the local network.

